  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader of a topic or an MP, I want each message clearly delimited from the next, so that I see where a message ends without looking for the avatar and signature lines. Operator feedback after a device test, 2026-11-07, milestone M4.\n\n### Current\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Resources/reader.css:49`: the only boundary between messages is `border-bottom: 1px solid var(--separator)`.\n  - Light: #d1d1d6 on #fff, contrast ≈1.5:1.\n  - Dark: #38383a on #000, contrast ≈1.8:1.\n- The modern header tint is 3% of the accent (`:58-59`), almost invisible.\n\n### Legacy\n`style-liste-light.css:153-160` @ 2440d79 draws a near-black 1 px rule (`#202020`) above each message, plus a 38 px header band. The dark and OLED sheets use grey borders. The port weakened this without a GAP row.\n\n### HIG\n- Alternating colours are mentioned only for macOS multicolumn tables. iOS neither recommends nor forbids them.\n- Colours must work in light, dark and Increase Contrast (Color, Accessibility pages).\n\n### Proposal (operator's idea)\nCSS only, derived from the theme tokens, so it follows light, dark, the dark brightness slider, a future OLED theme and the classic style:\n\n```css\n:root { --alt-strength: 5%; --separator-strong: #c6c6c8;\n        --surface-alt: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) var(--alt-strength), var(--background)); }\n/* dark */ --alt-strength: 9%; --separator-strong: var(--app-dark-separator, #545458);\n@media (prefers-contrast: more) { /* 10% light, 16% dark */ }\n.message { padding: 1em 1em .85em; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--separator-strong); }\narticle.message:nth-of-type(even) { background: var(--surface-alt); }\n:where(article.message:nth-of-type(even)) :is(table.citation, table.oldcitation, table.quote, table.code, table.fixed) { background: var(--placeholder); }\n```\n\n- `nth-of-type` ignores `div.separator1`.\n- Header, `.me` and whitelist tints compose on top.\n- Check text contrast: `--secondary` on the alternate surface is ≈4.7:1 in light.\n\n### Acceptance\n- A web test (`ReaderInsetsWebTests`-style) reads `getComputedStyle` on articles 1 and 2, in light and dark.\n- A GAP row records the divergence.\n- Mac check: light, dark (brightness 0–150 %), classic, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type XL, topics and MPs.\n- Coordinate the token values with LOT-122 (#213).\n\nRouting: Sonnet 5.5 → Opus 5.5, effort S. Part of the visual consistency umbrella (linked from it).",
